      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To examine the relation between muscular tenderness and local muscular fatigue."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Before-after trial, measuring pressure pain thresholds and signs of local muscular fatigue by using surface electromyography before, after, 10 minutes after, and 20 minutes after intervention."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "University rehabilitation department in Sweden."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PARTICIPANTS",
          "content": "Nineteen female hospital cleaners with unilateral chronic shoulder pain for 1 year. No previous trauma, surgery, or signs of systemic or neurologic disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "Static abduction endurance test with submaximal unilateral activation of the trapezius and deltoid muscles."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "Pressure pain thresholds and electromyographic fatigue parameters (root mean square [RMS]; mean power frequency [MPF])."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Mean normalized pressure pain threshold values increased significantly (95% confidence interval [CI]) and lasted for 20 minutes: in the trapezius, threshold values increased to 115% to 120% (95% CI, 100%-140%; P=.04-.05); and in the deltoid, the threshold increased to 112% to 115% (95% CI, 100%-130%; P=.02-.05). Development of significant electromyographically defined fatigue was seen: in the trapezius, the RMS increased to 130% (95% CI, 119%-141%), and in the deltoid, the MPF decreased to 78% (95% CI, 74%-82%), but normalized within 15 seconds to 10 minutes."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Lasting bilateral increases in pressure pain thresholds but transient local muscular fatigue were seen after a unilateral static endurance test. The sensitivity of the sensory nervous system may change during a static muscle contraction and sometimes contributes to a localized sensation of numbness."
        }
      ]},
